# Arduino-Based Smart Door Lock System

## 1. Abstract

The Arduino-Based Smart Door Lock System is an embedded security application designed to provide secure access control using password authentication. The system utilizes an Arduino Uno, a 4×4 keypad, a 16×2 LCD display, and a servo motor to control door locking and unlocking operations. Users can enter a predefined password through the keypad to gain access. The system also supports password modification and includes a security lockout feature that activates after three consecutive incorrect password attempts. This project demonstrates the practical application of embedded systems, user authentication, and actuator control in modern security systems.

---

## 2. Introduction

Security is an important requirement in homes, offices, laboratories, and industrial environments. Traditional mechanical locks can be vulnerable to unauthorized access and key duplication. Electronic door lock systems provide a more secure and flexible solution.

This project implements a password-protected door lock system using Arduino. A keypad is used for password entry, while an LCD display provides user feedback. A servo motor acts as the locking mechanism, allowing the door to unlock when the correct password is entered and automatically relock after a specified period.

